  "issue": {
    "body": "```python\r\nfrom starlette.applications import Starlette\r\nfrom starlette.testclient import TestClient\r\nfrom starlette.responses import PlainTextResponse\r\n\r\n\r\nasync def unhandled_exception_handler(request, e):\r\n    print(\"hey\")\r\n    return PlainTextResponse(\"hello\")\r\n\r\n\r\nclass App(Starlette):\r\n    def __init__(self):\r\n        super().__init__()\r\n        self.add_exception_handler(Exception, unhandled_exception_handler)\r\n\r\n\r\napp = App()\r\n\r\n\r\n@app.route(\"/method1\")\r\ndef http_method2(request):\r\n    raise Exception\r\n\r\n\r\ntest_cli = TestClient(app)\r\nprint(\"caught\", test_cli.get(\"/method1\"))\r\nprint(\"end\")\r\n```\r\n\r\n`hey` in exception handler is printed. `caught` and `end` are not printed.\r\n\r\nIf we just run in uvicorn instead of test client, browser returns `hello` as expected.",
    "closed_at": "2019-02-13T05:49:00Z",
